    <h1>Jian Loong Liew</h1>
    <p>I am based in Melbourne. I currently work as a Site Reliability Engineer at ANZ, mostly on automation and Google Cloud. Before that I taught software engineering at Monash University, which is still the job that trained my patience.</p>
    <p>On the side I like data visualisation, small public APIs, and tools that stay simple on purpose. Malaysia API, a browser sentiment analyser, a D3 word cloud, and Robogo (a YAML automation runner in Go) are the ones I still point people at. I have also spent too many evenings crawling r/AmItheAsshole and putting the results on a Raspberry Pi.</p>
    <p>I am not a Rustacean or a Gopher yet, though Robogo is doing its best to change the second one. I care about readable YAML, static files when a database is unnecessary, and writing that still works when the diagrams fall off.</p>
    <p>If you want to talk about reliability, teaching, or a half-finished visualisation, write to me.</p>
